        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Rhys-Davies, Timothy Dalton, Samuel L. Jackson, Peter Berg, Damon Wayans, Jeff Goldblum, Jon Lovitz, Cheech Marin, Salli Richardson, Jamie Foxx, Ian Fleming\n- Works: The Untouchables, Shōgun, Sliders, Robin of Sherwood, The Living Daylights, I, Claudius, The Great White Hype, James Bond\n- Roles: Agent Michael Malone, Pilot Vasco Rodrigues, Professor Maximillian Arturo, King Richard I, General Leonid Pushkin, Macro, James Bond\n- Organizations: SPECTRE, MI6\n- Concepts: fictional organization, film series, remake, miniseries, television series, video games\n\nFacts:\n- John Rhys-Davies played Macro in I, Claudius.\n- John Rhys-Davies played Pilot Vasco Rodrigues in the miniseries Shōgun.\n- John Rhys-Davies played King Richard I in Robin of Sherwood.\n- The Living Daylights was released in 1987 as the fifteenth entry in the James Bond film series.\n- The Living Daylights was the first James Bond film to star Timothy Dalton as MI6 agent James Bond.\n- John Rhys-Davies played General Leonid Pushkin in the James Bond film The Living Daylights.\n- John Rhys-Davies played Agent Michael Malone in the 1993 remake of the 1950s television series The Untouchables.\n- John Rhys-Davies played Professor Maximillian Arturo in Sliders.\n- The Great White Hype stars Samuel L. Jackson, Peter Berg, Damon Wayans, Jeff Goldblum, Jon Lovitz, Cheech Marin, John Rhys-Davies, Salli Richardson, and Jamie Foxx.\n- SPECTRE is a fictional organization featured in Ian Fleming's James Bond novels, the films based on those novels, and James Bond video games.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
